      "text": "To solve this problem, we must count the number of different valid configurations for coloring the small hexagons of the figure (which is a T-shape, as it seems). There are several constraints we must keep in mind:\n- Each small hexagon is must be colored either red, yellow, or green, a total of 3 colors.\n- We cannot color a hexagon the same color as one of the adjacent hexagons.\nSo, the most straightforward approach to this problem is to take cases.\n\nBefore proceeding to solve this problem with a combinatorial argument, finding a pattern might be easier and faster. One may notice that if we start with the provided configuration, there are 2 or the diagonals of the top triangle that cannot be the same color as their neighbors. \nSo, labeling the hexagons with six letters, ab, cd, e, fg, ha, this restricts 3, 4 and 4 possibilities of colors.\nSince each RHS element connects 2 small hexagons(this counts if they are consecutive), there are three possible cases:\n- Colors are not connected(2*4+2*2)= armetation, or 8 compositions of the 6 different hexagon elements.\n- Three hexagons of the same color(1X2 possible ways, because the middle hexagon can be connected by two different corners of the \"arm\" that connects them together).\n- There must be two sides connected by the same coloring.\n\nFor case one, each arm may contain 1 yellow, green, and yellow (2 and 3 combinations), and the rest are determined by the way colorful arms are chosen. Similarly, in case two, there are also 2 and 3 possible combos for coloring the arm, 6 possible compositions of combos (1 arm and 2 arm cases cannot occur), 2 possible arms that start, and there are 3 combinations as above, and, (3X2+2X2)=10 final combinations. In case three, if you color 2 hexagons the same color, it is not possible to choose a different coloring scheme for the third one. \nThus, we have a total of: 8+10+10=28 different colors; [asy]\npath a=(0,0)--(10,0)--(15,8.7)--(10,17.3)--(0,17.3)--(-5,8.7)--cycle;\ndraw(a);\ndraw(shift((15,8.7))*a);\ndraw(shift((15,-8.7))*a);\ndraw(shift((30,17.3))*a);\ndraw(shift((30,0))*a);\ndraw(shift((30,-17.3))*a);\ndraw(shift((45,26))*a);\ndraw(shift((45,8.7))*a);\ndraw(shift((45,-8.7))*a);\ndraw(shift((60,17.3))*a);\ndraw(shift((60,0))*a);\ndraw(shift((60,-17.3))*a);\ndraw(shift((75,8.7))*a);\ndraw(shift((75,-8.7))*a);\ndot((-7,17.3));dot((7,17.3));dot((-7,-8.7));dot((-7,8.7));dot((7,-8.7));dot((7,8.7));[/asy]",
